{"panel_html": "<section class=\"panel rel-scope active\" id=\"panel-container\" data-rel=\"{}\"><div class=\"scroll-hint\">Scroll right for more semesters \u2192</div><div class=\"flow-scroll\"><div class=\"flow-container\">\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 1</span><span class=\"col-term\">Fall</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;UB Seminar: a 1- or 3-credit seminar every student completes in their first semester of enrollment, taught by faculty across departments around a &#x27;big idea&#x27; in the discipline. A UB Curriculum core requirement, not specific to this major.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/seminar.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">UB Seminar</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introductory Psychology&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;General survey of perception; learning and memory; cognitive, developmental, personality, abnormal, and social psychology; and behavioral neuroscience. Requires participation in research or a short paper.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer, Winter&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">PSY 101LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Introductory Psychology</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Introduction to Health and Human Services&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Studies the health and human service system in the United States and locally, as it has been affected by history, changing values, and changes in the economic and political environment. Particularly emphasizes the gerontological, childhood, and community mental health service systems.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer, Winter&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">SSC 103SEM</span><span class=\"box-title\">Introduction to Health and Human Services</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"or-group\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Writing and Rhetoric&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;An introduction to research, writing, and rhetorical practices employed in academic and professional contexts. The course examines the operation of genres, the audiences they address, and the purposes they serve. The course focuses on the analysis and development of student writing and rhetorical practice. Assignments include research essays, digital compositions, and oral presentations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;ENG 105 non-Z Requisite&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">ENG 105LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Writing and Rhetoric</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div><div class=\"or-sep\">or</div><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-3-1\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"health-and-human-services-ba-community-mental-health-concentration-social-work-msw__box-0-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &q